  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Premier Marketing Services (PMS) Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nutritious mushrooms can deliver &apos;wealth and health&apos; to growers and consumers. Mushroom farming requires little space or equipment, therefore it is perfectly suited to people without assets. The project will tackle the main barriers identified to mushrooms becoming a vibrant industry in Ghana. The Association knows that existing members grow less than a quarter of what they could if their Association were stronger, could centrally negotiate bulk contracts and reduce waste. It will establish a central marketing service to sell, guarantee quality and consumers&apos; safety. It will also offer micro-credits and record-keeping training; additionally, it will develop and trial an intensive training approach with a pilot group of existing growers, then roll this out in all regions where there are members. The project will help the Association to invest, speed up spawn delivery, assure members get quality spawn and earn an income for the Association itself.</narrative>
  </description>
